  "metric_explanation": {
    "title": "Why ROC-AUC and PR-AUC Are the Definitive Metrics in Target Discovery",
    "summary": "In biomedical pairwise screening and oncology drug discovery, datasets suffer from severe class imbalance. A naive baseline that blindly predicts all pairs as active achieves high nominal accuracy while failing to distinguish true synergistic drugs from unviable candidates. ROC-AUC measures the ranking probability: the likelihood that the model assigns a higher compatibility score to an active pair than a discontinued/failed pair across all decision thresholds. PR-AUC (Precision-Recall Area) measures positive class precision without being inflated by true negatives, making it the most critical indicator for clinical pipeline selection."
  }
